{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru","id":1058167,"title":"A Maurader guru?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-04T15:11:13-08:00","id":1058167,"title":"A Maurader guru?","content":"I thought up a antagonist for a Mage chronicle. It is a Marauder who is the head of a cult and acts as a guru and a prophet for the cult's god. How could this work in Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:16:19-08:00","id":1058169,"title":"","content":"So what's his deal as a Marauder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:15:47-08:00","id":1058205,"title":"","content":"He genuinely believes he is a prophet. His insanity goes so far that he actually hears voices in his head and thinks they are the voices of his gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:46:09-08:00","id":1058217,"title":"","content":"You know you could just make the gods real &quot;incarna level spirits&quot; and skip the marauder bit. Saying he's just a Skitzo is a lame marauder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:55:20-08:00","id":1058222,"title":"","content":"Sounds fun enough.<br /> I guess there are tons of ways to go with this.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining the divine prophecies and manifestations are a subtle reflection of the marauder's subconscious, taking from his/her vision of the world as it is and as it should be, optimistic ideals, desires, fears, and sometimes just things the marauder experiences. Maybe a mage close enough to the marauder would be able to recognize this.<br /> <br /> So, you could run this as anything from a crazy death or doomsday cult, to some sort of isolationist group trying to establish a holy utopia, to someone trying to right the wrongs of the world in accordance to the dictates of the higher power, an unstable marauder who genuinely wants to help people and has uplifted the spirits and lives of the downtrodden and called them on some grand exodus, all sorts of things really. I guess a lot depends on the tone you want to establish.<br /> <br /> Apart from magick-fueled miracles and divine manifestations that are likely to cause investigation by the Traditions or Technocracy, you could actually even build up this marauder's &quot;church&quot; and give them a few holy items of power, maybe some disciple types, and maybe even genuine heroes who would die for their beliefs and for the greater good.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T18:36:58-08:00","id":1058237,"title":"","content":"I could definitely see the Marauder being a person who thinks what they are doing is for the greater good. Unfortunately, their definition for the greater good is having their followers do crimes like assault, murder and white collar crime. I can picture a scene where the PCs are chasing down a guy who gunned down their contact only to have him disappear in a bright light, no doubt sent by his Marauder master. Now that leads me to a other question, what exactly should the Marauder's god be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T23:33:03-08:00","id":1058308,"title":"","content":"What I'm missing in the discussion is the actual defining Marauder aspect.<br /> <br /> Because this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058205#post1058205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He genuinely believes he is a prophet. His insanity goes so far that he actually hears voices in his head and thinks they are the voices of his gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can in theory happen to anybody who suddenly awakens, and their (high level) avatar poses and looks like a deity in their eyes, *especially* if they have the 'Manifest Avatar' merit.<br /> The Avatar becomes a holy figure trying to teach them and make them teach others. Heck, it's the concept of a Verbena of mine, to whom their avatar appears as the actual trifold Goddess, and they see themselves as their priestess. She's not a Marauder - but what would *you* do if the deity you believe in actually appears and talks to you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So yeah, I think a servant of a God like that does not quite equal Marauder. It *can*, of course. It can. The symptoms and actions can be the same on the outside. But you need to decide wether it's just a Mage with delusions, or an actual paradox-chewing dynamic Marauder or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T03:46:03-08:00","id":1058346,"title":"","content":"Good points but I think we should be suggesting how to make this work as an actual marauder.<br /> <br /> Like the sort that if you actually talked to the &quot;real&quot; god/spirit being worshiped, the god would have no idea what the marauder was smoking and why he's using the god's name falsely... and all those angels (or prophets, or lesser divinities, or whatnot) are just things in the guy's head fueled by his own magick and some of the miraculous stories regarding his religion didn't even happen anywhere but in his head.<br /> <br /> If it were me, I'd run it as a marauder prophet of a nonexistent benevolent god with grand miracles, divine spirits, and great epic stories that none of the mages of any religion and numerous spirits have ever even heard about. Heck, I'd have some spirits asking the mages to have him investigated and run it as a sort of mystery game. Throw in a spirit that wants to pose as the god or one of its servants, some choristers who want to meddle, and actual faithful followers and I think it could make for an interesting game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T05:36:12-08:00","id":1058369,"title":"","content":"The Avatar could make a decent god. But, would that mean that he and his followers would basically be worshipping a extension of himself? Also, I figured that making him a Marauder would allow him to do &quot;miracles&quot; in front of his followers. I will also consider the nonexistent god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T05:37:14-08:00","id":1058370,"title":"","content":"I think them being a Marauder Antagonist is a neat idea, since it means that they can show the divine displeasure against the PCs through redirected Paradox. He can perform a miracle of incredible power and then laugh as the &quot;heathens&quot; are twisted into horrific shapes as backlash.<br /> <br /> Personally my take is that ALL Mages with Personified Avatars are at least a tad insane, since their Avatars are just dead Angel Corpses that they've projected personalities onto. Marauder is just the supernatural insanity that comes with having twisted reality to the point of losing track of the illusion of sanity. Marauders aren't extra insane IMO, they've just given up on the idea of sanity being a thing almost. That's why they don't get Paradox Backlash; they don't buy into the idea of a rational reality striking back at them when they do crazy things with Magick. Why does it hit others? Because they still subscribe to the idea that Paradoxic backlashes are a fundamental part of reality. In a very sad and broken way, Marauders have &quot;ascended&quot;, since they no longer need to fear Paradox. However the price of admission is the belief that they are sane, which is a valuable delusion for Mages as it lets them exist &quot;normally&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:33:31-08:00","id":1058395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058370#post1058370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally my take is that ALL Mages with Personified Avatars are at least a tad insane, since their Avatars are just dead Angel Corpses that they've projected personalities onto.</div> </div> </div> </div>Althouth this may be part of Demon the Fallen lore, this is NOT part of Mage cannon, so do not take it as it is. The Avatar in Mage is a mysterious part of the soul without a proper definition or proper understanding of what it truly is. You can even say that Avatars are &quot;angelic spiritual detritus&quot; if you wanna in your game, but you can't take it as cannon lore for the game Mage Ascension (even if you can for Demon)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:35:50-08:00","id":1058396,"title":"","content":"And who said that Maradeurs are immune to Paradox? They aren't, it just works different from them (and to their benefit, mostly - except when the Paradox ejects you from reality fully)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:22:04-08:00","id":1058418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058396#post1058396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And who said that Maradeurs are immune to Paradox? They aren't, it just works different from them (and to their benefit, mostly - except when the Paradox ejects you from reality fully)</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that when Backlash hits them, it seeks out the nearest target other than the Marauder? Like nearby Mages and Night Folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:25:11-08:00","id":1058420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058395#post1058395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Althouth this may be part of Demon the Fallen lore, this is NOT part of Mage cannon, so do not take it as it is. The Avatar in Mage is a mysterious part of the soul without a proper definition or proper understanding of what it truly is. You can even say that Avatars are &quot;angelic spiritual detritus&quot; if you wanna in your game, but you can't take it as cannon lore for the game Mage Ascension (even if you can for Demon)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, it's just the way I like to run it. Truth doesn't matter that much in my games though, since the belief that your Avatar is a Goddess called Risk is a powerful one that lets you take over a city, doesn't matter if Risk is actually the rotting celestial corpse of the Angel who created Grasslands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:43:26-08:00","id":1058472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058418#post1058418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read that when Backlash hits them, it seeks out the nearest target other than the Marauder? Like nearby Mages and Night Folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is described on pages 56-58 of Book of Madness rev. First of all, the Marauder will get one temporary Quiety rating everytime he botches a Vulgar Magik; Quiets of 6+ will cause him to get ejected from the Tellurian as the unnatural aliens they are, usually straight to the Deep Umbra, from where most can never return (Hmm... That just gave me an idea... Maybe the monstruousities, the cthonic titans trying to shatter the Dream Shell that protects us from the beyond, maybe they are expeled Marauders? That could be interesting...)<br /> <br /> Secondly, when Marauders are to take a backlash, you take the degree of the backlash and subtracts from his temporary Quiet. Thats how much will hit the Marauder, the rest go to the nearest awakened (or even sleeper, if no awaken is around; nightfolk count as sleepers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:47:04-08:00","id":1058474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058472#post1058472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is described on pages 56-58 of Book of Madness rev. First of all, the Marauder will get one temporary Quiety rating everytime he botches a Vulgar Magik; Quiets of 6+ will cause him to get ejected from the Tellurian as the unnatural aliens they are, usually straight to the Deep Umbra, from where most can never return (Hmm... That just gave me an idea... Maybe the monstruousities, the cthonic titans trying to shatter the Dream Shell that protects us from the beyond, maybe they are expeled Marauders? That could be interesting...)<br /> <br /> Secondly, when Marauders are to take a backlash, you take the degree of the backlash and subtracts from his temporary Quiet. Thats how much will hit the Marauder, the rest go to the nearest awakened (or even sleeper, if no awaken is around; nightfolk count as sleepers)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then, judicious use of Prime can quite easily keep a Marauder with tiny backlashes and let everyone else around them take the worst of it. There's a reason M20 says that only the most experienced and sensible and trusted of players should be allowed to play as a Marauder, since it's ripe for abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:05:27-08:00","id":1058483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058369#post1058369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Avatar could make a decent god. But, would that mean that he and his followers would basically be worshipping a extension of himself? Also, I figured that making him a Marauder would allow him to do &amp;quot;miracles&amp;quot; in front of his followers. I will also consider the nonexistent god?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the followers believe he can make miracles, he can make miracles...<br /> <br /> 100 acolytes that believe in the stunts the Mage can pull, will make your magik coincidental, no need to be Marauder (as long as there is no unbelievers around). <br /> <br /> In the case of a Marauder, its not that his followers would believe he can make miracles, but <b>everybody</b> inside his reality bubble would believe that <b>miracles are common day-to-day routine</b>. People passing by on the street would say &quot;nah, another prophet healing the sick, how boring&quot;, and wouldn't remember a thing after leaving the distorted reality bubble.<br /> <br /> So.... It would be hard for the Marauder to have a cult <u>outside his reality bubble</u>. As soon people left his crazy reality, they would forget the whole mess.<br /> <br /> What could happen, however, is that ANY sleeper that crossed inside his bubble, would INSTANTLY start worshiping him as a prophet... No rolls, no effects, no nothing. Its simply a new reality - in his twisted perception of the world, the Marauder leads an Exodus, so, ANY sleeper that enters, simply conforms to the new reality. This is NOT brainwashing or something like it... The ENTIRE history of the sleeper works differently inside the bubble (inside the bubble, Mr John Smith is not a banker with 2 kids and a ex wife living in Sidney, in this bubble of reality he is Abdah, who spent 40 years in the desert following the prophet to the promised land). <br /> <br /> The Marauder can give orders to his &quot;flock&quot; to leave his bubble (my trusted beloved Abdah, go now to the lands of Egypt, and tell the Paraoh that we are leaving!), but as soon as the sleeper lefts the twisted bubble, his former identity returns, without any knowledge of the time under the distorted reality (if Abdah leaves, he will be John Smith, the banker, once again, and will have no idea what happened to him in the last 40 years that he was out... Specially if he still have his 30 years, if he thinks its still may 03 of 1977 and his two daughters are over 50 years old now...)<br /> <br /> And... A prophet probably wouldn't command assassinations. Thats not the way of gods. A true god would commit mass genocide, not minor murders.<br /> <br /> This would be more fitting for a dark prophet who thinks himself the emissary of some great evil or some demonic being. (Gods are more direct and far, far worse than any demon of lore)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:08:45-08:00","id":1058486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058369#post1058369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, would that mean that he and his followers would basically be worshipping a extension of himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every little bit of the reality around a Marauder is just an extension of themselves. Marauders are basically lost in a solipsistic instance, where all reality exists only as a fillament of their wills.<br /> <br /> Thats why they are anatema to consensual reality after all, and thats the reason the very Tellurian rejects their existence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:28:59-08:00","id":1058494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058474#post1058474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well then, judicious use of Prime can quite easily keep a Marauder with tiny backlashes and let everyone else around them take the worst of it. There's a reason M20 says that only the most experienced and sensible and trusted of players should be allowed to play as a Marauder, since it's ripe for abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Play a Marauder?<br /> <br /> Well... Just dont botch 5 times, or you're out... Literally out... Of everything...<br /> <br /> First of all, the Marauder would need a reason to use Prime for that. Why would he try to minimaze his own backlashes, since they probably are the most natural occurances to them? You see, a Quiet 5 VA who thinks his in a Virtual Reality game, will not think that he &quot;should minimize his backlashes&quot;... Thats cheating!!! You'll never get to the end of the game by shitting!<br /> <br /> Now, all those &quot;sleepers&quot;, you know of course that they are just NPCs algorithms... Its not real people!<br /> <br /> And those &quot;Mages&quot; who call themselves &quot;hermetics, akashics&quot; and say &quot;they wanna to help you&quot;...<br /> <br /> You know they are all bossess right?<br /> <br /> Kill them and loot their corpses to advance to the next level.<br /> <br /> Have you ever played an immersive RPG v\u00eddeo game, like Skyrim (and others Elders Scrolls) or any of the Fallout?<br /> <br /> Now, imagine a Marauder that thinks the real world is just a Fallout game (damn, he may even use Time 3 to &quot;reload previous save point).<br /> <br /> Did you ever got into a town on Fallout or Skyrim, and just murdered the ENTIRE town, just because you were bored and for the fun to see &quot;people&quot; running for their lives? (Yeah, I know... But I can bet EVERYBODY do that, once in a while).<br /> <br /> Well, the VA Marauder do that too...<br /> <br /> There is even a movie EXACTLY like that, know I can't remember the name, but its an interactive virtual reality game, were each player takes an specific role, and in the end, the players couldn't tell reality and game apart anymore. <br /> <br /> Did you ever considered that those people whose lives you're impacting on Fallout could be REAL people?<br /> <br /> So, when playing Fallout, you can enter some codes to avoid damage. But thats cheating.<br /> <br /> When you use a grenade, you know it can cause you damage, so you better use it with the uttermost care.<br /> <br /> The same goes for Vulgar effects.<br /> <br /> And the backlash is not &quot;Paradox effect&quot;. Its &quot;game design&quot;, or &quot;god/devils will&quot;, or, if you believe you're a superhero, its &quot;another trick from my archrival, the clockmaker&quot; (and you'll see a cynical smile in vanishing in the shadowns, along the noise of several clocks vanishing in the distance). Of course, &quot;game design&quot;, &quot;god's will&quot; and the &quot;clockmaker's tricks&quot; also persecute the &quot;game bossess/major-allied-NPC&quot;, &quot;other prophets/false prophets&quot; and the heroe's &quot;sidekicks/rival villains&quot; too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:34:02-08:00","id":1058496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Origin