e each player takes an specific role, and in the end, the players couldn't tell reality and game apart anymore.<br /> <br /> Did you ever considered that those people whose lives you're impacting on Fallout could be REAL people?<br /> <br /> So, when playing Fallout, you can enter some codes to avoid damage. But thats cheating.<br /> <br /> When you use a grenade, you know it can cause you damage, so you better use it with the uttermost care.<br /> <br /> The same goes for Vulgar effects.<br /> <br /> And the backlash is not &quot;Paradox effect&quot;. Its &quot;game design&quot;, or &quot;god/devils will&quot;, or, if you believe you're a superhero, its &quot;another trick from my archrival, the clockmaker&quot; (and you'll see a cynical smile in vanishing in the shadowns, along the noise of several clocks vanishing in the distance). Of course, &quot;game design&quot;, &quot;god's will&quot; and the &quot;clockmaker's tricks&quot; also persecute the &quot;game bossess/major-allied-NPC&quot;, &quot;other prophets/false prophets&quot; and the heroe's &quot;sidekicks/rival villains&quot; too</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I really like this, but you're ignoring that Marauders can be ALMOST sane and remain that way for a long time. At the lower levels of Quiet they're a long way off &quot;Wow, Elder Scrolls: New York is amazing!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:46:49-08:00","id":1058504,"title":"","content":"You know, maybe I should make the guru a Nephandi. It would probably make more sense since Nephandi's are prone to starting cults. He would either be a Infernalist or a K'llasshaa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:52:33-08:00","id":1058506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058496#post1058496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I really like this, but you're ignoring that Marauders can be ALMOST sane and remain that way for a long time. At the lower levels of Quiet they're a long way off &amp;quot;Wow, Elder Scrolls: New York is amazing!&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Quiet 1 and 2 are livable, 3 and 4 is problematic, 5 is deep shit alien crazy, and 6+ is safe because they press the eject buttom by themselves. Quiet 1 is really minor stuff, like a british marauder that makes the drivers seat changes on every car around here (sleepers dont notice it, but other Mages do) and stuff like it. Still, remember that all the backlashes the Marauder suffers will only be reduced by his quiet level (not so much for the Quiet 1 almost sane guy). That means that, the more sane the guy, the more subjected to Paradox; the most powerful ones are those things in the Deep Umbra with more than 6 Quiet (those really are almost immune to backlashes, however, they probably can't even have a permanent form in a space/time reality).<br /> <br /> So, in the case of the british Marauder, his backlashes would take the form of Her Majesty guards showing to arrest him (or the poor awaken sods around taking some of his backlashes) for his crimes against the crown, or some irishes of the IRA shooting him on the street for confusing him with an agent of the MRi-6, holligans trying to get him after a Liverpool game or even Ze Germans coming with tanks... Or perhaps its just all that indian spyce burning his guts.<br /> <br /> Anyway, ANY backlashes for a Marauder, would be something built to fit its mindscape solipsistic self narrative.<br /> <br /> Thats actually, one of the reasons why other mages think that Marauders are immune to Paradox (they can't distinguish the backlashes from the underlying alternative reality)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T12:11:26-08:00","id":1058512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058504#post1058504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, maybe I should make the guru a Nephandi. It would probably make more sense since Nephandi's are prone to starting cults. He would either be a Infernalist or a K'llasshaa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not a bad idea to have a Marauder guru, I found it fantastic, much more interesting than the typical &quot;full evil Nefandi with the cult of cuckos&quot;. The Marauder's Avatar, this guy would be sweet to buy &quot;Manifest Avatar&quot; and other merrits/flaws just like it... His Avatar could be an &quot;emissary of the God(s)&quot; (or so does the Avatar AND the Mage thinks), like the Archangel Michael (Gabrielites? Yeah, Im convinced that those guys are NUTS), or it could be Hermes, Eshu, maybe it could be a whirlpool of energetic thunders and lights that can commune DIRECTLY with the Wyld... The Marauder (and the unfortunate sleepers enthralled by this bubble to serve as cultists) would take their orders DIRECTLY from the Avatar, that could command all kind of nonsense (this type of ridiculous stupid things is not uncommon on religions - who think its normal to cut off the skin of your dick? Or to be forbidden to eat shrimp or work on sundays? Or to bath in a dirt river like the Ganges?) Let the avatar tell them to cut their little fingers off, to walk with only one feet with shoes and the other naked, to bath on the Tamisa, pray every midnights or jerk off in every public toilets... Anything you'd want, from the pratical to the total ridiculously commic, to the psychotic dangerous.<br /> <br /> After, you dont discuss with god, you just do its bidding.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> When some weird voices inside of your head, claiming they are the voice of god, when they tell you &quot;kill your only son for me&quot;.<br /> <br /> What do you do?<br /> <br /> You take your best cuttler and tire your moda fucking son on a rock to butcher him to please the Lord.<br /> <br /> Just like Abraham did.<br /> <br /> And thats what a Marauder do too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:24:24-08:00","id":1058539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058496#post1058496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I really like this, but you're ignoring that Marauders can be ALMOST sane and remain that way for a long time. At the lower levels of Quiet they're a long way off &quot;Wow, Elder Scrolls: New York is amazing!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine the spells.<br /> <br /> Complete Quest.<br /> Matter 2/Prime 2/Mind 3<br /> <br /> After returning to someone you have aided in some trivial task. A monetary reward will appear on their person, one they always intended to give you for your help. I mean, it's totally normal to pay someone $200 for taking their neighbor for a walk right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:30:01-08:00","id":1058542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058539#post1058539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine the spells.<br /> <br /> Complete Quest.<br /> Matter 2/Prime 2/Mind 3<br /> <br /> After returning to someone you have aided in some trivial task. A monetary reward will appear on their person, one they always intended to give you for your help. I mean, it's totally normal to pay someone $200 for taking their neighbor for a walk right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm loving that concept! So someone Awakens believing that they're the Beta Tester of a new VR Game, and their Avatar is the User Interface and Player Guide.<br /> <br /> Correspondence can create a glowing path to your destination. Time allows you to &quot;Wait&quot; for 12 hours without experiencing anything in the meantime. Correspondence allows for Fast Travel. Mind allows you to remember every quest given to you and every bit of map you've explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:31:52-08:00","id":1058544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058539#post1058539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine the spells.<br /> <br /> Complete Quest.<br /> Matter 2/Prime 2/Mind 3<br /> <br /> After returning to someone you have aided in some trivial task. A monetary reward will appear on their person, one they always intended to give you for your help. I mean, it's totally normal to pay someone $200 for taking their neighbor for a walk right?</div> </div> </div> </div>SavePoint<br /> <br /> Time 5, Life 3, Entropy 2, Mind 1<br /> <br /> Yeah, you do know what I mean... In case of death, respawn from your last save point... You damn immortal cheater...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:34:35-08:00","id":1058549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058544#post1058544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SavePoint<br /> <br /> Time 5, Life 3, Entropy 2, Mind 1<br /> <br /> Yeah, you do know what I mean... In case of death, respawn from your last save point... You damn immortal cheater...</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you need some spirit to fire your immortal soul back in time to your body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:36:49-08:00","id":1058550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058549#post1058549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't you need some spirit to fire your immortal soul back in time to your body?</div> </div> </div> </div>The descriptions of Time wouldn't say it so. Thats the better version, mind you, the easier version takes only Time 3, but you'll just &quot;reload&quot; your game a few seconds before death, so, be ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:41:40-08:00","id":1058554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058550#post1058550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The descriptions of Time wouldn't say it so. Thats the better version, mind you, the easier version takes only Time 3, but you'll just &quot;reload&quot; your game a few seconds before death, so, be ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are you activating Time after you die? I swear the reason you need Spirit, Mind and Life to do the &quot;undo your death&quot; thing is because those are mandatory components to reverse time without your body (Spirit), and bring your Mind back to your earlier body (Mind and Life).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:44:56-08:00","id":1058556,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I think you should really watch this movie<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Existenz\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/76/EXISTENZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Existenz\" target=\"_blank\"> Existenz - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Existenz\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Existenz </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> When the characters are inside the game, they dont act as humans, but rather, they keep to their scripts.<br /> <br /> Thats what sleepers inside reality bubbles of Marauders will do too. Just like those pesk Fallout NPCS that won't talk to you unless its in their script... A &quot;non quest&quot; sleeper inside such a nightmare will just answer &quot;howdy&quot; to you, but it won't even look at your eyes if you ask him about a talking white dog... And, there is a high propability that some floating warnings will appear in from of you if you take so much as a cup from a table at a bar (well, you'll habe to use Entropy 1 to know which items are &quot;Green&quot; and which are &quot;Red&quot;). And remember, if you take a forbidden item while inside the Marauder's &quot;Elder Scrolls: New York&quot;, a bunch of cops will show with a simple offer to you: surrender and go to jail (or bribe them, if this is your first offense) or die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:48:42-08:00","id":1058557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058554#post1058554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are you activating Time after you die? I swear the reason you need Spirit, Mind and Life to do the &amp;quot;undo your death&amp;quot; thing is because those are mandatory components to reverse time without your body (Spirit), and bring your Mind back to your earlier body (Mind and Life).</div> </div> </div> </div>This effect is made to be always on. You dont &quot;do it after dying&quot;; it just activate upon what would be death. Thats why Entropy 2. The moment you would die, is the moment you return. Its not ressurection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:54:23-08:00","id":1058559,"title":"","content":"In the &quot;Elder Scrolls: New York&quot;, Paradox backlashes are glitches in the game... Like that glitch of the immortal guard, or the Quest you can't complete, making you stuck in the story, or that one that makes you enter a wall, but you can never leave, and end up stuck in a blackness portion of unmade algorithm... (Ejected to the Deep Umbra?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:22:33-08:00","id":1058605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058557#post1058557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This effect is made to be always on. You dont &quot;do it after dying&quot;; it just activate upon what would be death. Thats why Entropy 2. The moment you would die, is the moment you return. Its not ressurection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, Time 4 + Entropy 2/3 allows the caster to &quot;hang&quot; the spell, which will go off if a designated event transpires. In this case, when the caster dies. Time 4 doesn't care about the state of the mage who cast it; some place, objects, or family lines have enchantments hung on them from centuries ago, waiting for the moment when their trigger occurs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:15:57-08:00","id":1058632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058167-a-maurader-guru?p=1058605#post1058605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically, Time 4 + Entropy 2/3 allows the caster to &amp;quot;hang&amp;quot; the spell, which will go off if a designated event transpires. In this case, when the caster dies. Time 4 doesn't care about the state of the mage who cast it; some place, objects, or family lines have enchantments hung on them from centuries ago, waiting for the moment when their trigger occurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, it would be Time 4. This would be a &quot;reset to last auto save&quot;. (Meaning: in case you die for whatever reason, the &quot;game will load&quot; a few turns back... The *gamer* must be careful thou, because &quot;resetting the game&quot; too often can cause severe &quot;game glitches&quot; - that can bug the NPCs or the Player - you really dont wanna screw with your auto save do you?)<br /> <br /> Time 5 can let you set a save point manually, wich you can use at any moment to &quot;load your game&quot; to; the *gamer* must be warned however, that he will lose all his progress at the game after that point. Using too many save points can also induce glitches","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:36:28-08:00","id":1058645,"title":"","content":"Time 2 - Watch quests scripts.<br /> As a beta tester of the game, you can look into the games code sources to get a glimpse of the next step required to any of your active quests in the game, or to see all the avaiable quests at the moment.<br /> <br /> Mind 1 - Game Map<br /> You better have a Game Map for your travels inside the game. You open the Map menu with this command.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 3 - Fast Travel<br /> No need to walk all that map all the time. With this you can fast travel to any location that you have already unlocked in your map.<br /> Be careful thou, Fast Travel is still prone to glitches in the beta version<br /> <br /> Pinpoint Active Quest - Correspondence 1, Entropy 1<br /> Gets an arrow pointing you the direction of your next quest objective; very, very useful.<br /> <br /> Update Map - Correpondence 1<br /> From time to time, NPCs may talk about important places of interest; some times they'll talk to you, sometimes they'll talk amongst themselves. Whenever you get one of those precious informations, use this to mark the location on your game map<br /> <br /> Development experimental area - Spirit 3<br /> Allows you to enter the Developers section, which have a LOT of debbuged areas, not programmed sections, as long as the many algorithms used in the game. Be careful when dealing with the core codes!<br /> <br /> Primal Decription - Prime 1<br /> Sometimes, you just gotta use some Primal Coding against the nastier NPCs out there. This is the basics of it - it allows you to see any Primal Codes in the area; this will help you decripting their sources, and you can even trace each Boss (Awakened) towards their signature code","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:32:47-08:00","id":1058839,"title":"","content":"Oh man. This discussion turned into awesome MMORG-Marauder rotes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually, it reminds me of Team 23.<br /> Team 23 is a bunch of (assumed VA) Marauders described in the Book of Madness Revised. They essentially were playing their Digital Web version of DooM co-op....when suddenly a massive paradox whiteout hit.<br /> <br /> And they have been playing ever since, except they're not in the Digital Web anymore.<br /> As in, they warp into your favorite office building, in full gamey scifi gear, and see all employees as monsters that need to be &quot;fragged&quot;. And then do so. And then leave on finishing the level. Yeeeah.<br /> Funnily enough, they don't attack Mages, and see them as other players they can have a chat with...even if it's just &quot;lol n00b!&quot;<br /> ( If you read up about them in Book of Madness Revised, also make sure to read the entry for &quot;Roy Baker&quot; )<br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <br /> Why do I bring this up? Because I'm imagining Mr. RPG/MORPG trying to get a party together... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> M20 and the book of Madness Revised both describe how merely being in the presence of a Marauder for prolonged time can pull you into their Quiet, and if said Marauder manages to get a few unawakened (generic NPC party mooks) and a couple of awakened (unique plot party characters if singleplayer RPG / other players if MMORPG) with them, things could get quite interesting..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-06-2017, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:01:50-08:00","id":1058849,"title":"","content":"Marauder rotes are awesome. For example, for the &quot;Movie Star&quot; Marauder (who believes it is constantly in a movie set)<br /> <br /> CUT! TAKE 2!!! - Time 4<br /> On many occasions, The Director (the avatar of the crazy Mage) will want to make interruptions on a scene, to garantee it is perfect. The rest of the cast knows that they must remain absolutely still, as to not spoil the scene. After talking to you and making all the needed adjustments, the scene will resume as normal. Just be careful that taking too many scenes is tiresome, which can lead to mistakes from the cast (Paradox).<br /> <br /> Effects, Less Blood please! - Life 2/3<br /> You dont wanna have to make the movie only for 18+ years old right? Luckly, special effects can deal with it. Be careful thou, this is an hard effect, and the guys are know for mistakes from time to time (Paradox).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:15:39-08:00","id":1058856,"title":"","content":"For the Marauder Prophet, that actually isn't such a deeper quiet. I would place it as 3 or 4 (the MMORPG and the Movie Star Marauders are both 5). This guy is much more straight foward in his madness and rotes of course unless if his temporary Quiet goes up to 5+, in which case he would start believing he is actually an angel of the Lord, and would start &quot;hunting the demons&quot;, which could be... Anyone... Sorta like the Ghost Rider from Marvel. Well, I actually had a Marauder like this in a game of mine as one major antagonistic villain, he believed himself to be an angel, and he were actually very effective at hunting nefandic forces... But it also let a pile of corpses of &quot;innocents&quot; (well, nobody is perfect, and while a few deserved that, many didnt... Cheating is terrible, but I dont think it should be dealt with death penalty. But... The Lord is mysterious after all)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}